From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:41:57 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] arcade-screen

Neo Geo, CPS1 and CPS2 each get their own Screen section, listed after
the 32X and shown only when the card holds sets for that board. Neo Geo
has Shader and Picture; CPS1 and CPS2 add Vertical Games. Shader walks
Off and the retro list into the board's own file; the in-game Shader row
and the shader shortcut walk the same list. Picture is the Mega Drive's,
Stretch by default, then Actual and 4:3, stored as neogeo, cps1 and cps2
in Config/picture.txt.

Vertical Games (Config/arcade.txt, cps1 and cps2) is Upright by default:
FBNeo asks for a quarter turn, slot answers it for the arcade boards only
and turns the frame itself, counter-clockwise, into a 3:4 picture in the
middle of a 3:2 canvas as tall as the board's long side (576x384 for
CPS), shown whole on the panel at 360x480. Turned leaves the frame as the
board draws it, sideways and filling the panel (FBNeo's vertical mode
"enabled"), and turns the D-pad with it for a handheld held with its
right edge up (Right is Up, Up is Left); every button stays where it is.
The choice applies from the next game and sets nothing for horizontal
games. Every other core is still refused quarter turns.
